
            documented in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#rightsWorkSet">lido:rightsWorkSet</a>&gt;.</p>
            <p><strong>Note on Rights Type</strong></p>
            <p>The &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#rightsType">lido:rightsType</a>&gt;
            element allows for indexing rights pertaining to each of the
            above information areas, i.e., the object or work, the
            record, and the resource. LIDO allows two distinct usages of
            this element: a <a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00920">generic
            type</a> statement designating the kind of right in
            question, e.g., copyright or performance right, and <a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00921">specific
            rights information</a>, such as a particular license. The
            values are provided by the LIDO <a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/rightsType_type">Rights
            Type Type-Vocabulary</a>.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> Following is an example of how
            to record a generic rights type.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb17"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb17-1"><a href="#cb17-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkWrap</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-2"><a href="#cb17-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-3"><a href="#cb17-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        <span class="co">&lt;!-- &quot;Generic rights type&quot; --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb17-4"><a href="#cb17-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsType</span></span>
<span id="cb17-5"><a href="#cb17-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">            lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00920&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-6"><a href="#cb17-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span></span>
<span id="cb17-7"><a href="#cb17-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                rdf:about=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300055598&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-8"><a href="#cb17-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span><span class="ot"> xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-9"><a href="#cb17-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                    copyright</span>
<span id="cb17-10"><a href="#cb17-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;/<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-11"><a href="#cb17-11" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsType</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-12"><a href="#cb17-12" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb17-13"><a href="#cb17-13" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkWrap</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> Following is an example of how
            to record specific rights information.</p>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb18"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb18-1"><a href="#cb18-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkWrap</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-2"><a href="#cb18-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-3"><a href="#cb18-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        <span class="co">&lt;!-- &quot;Specific rights information&quot; --&gt;</span></span>
<span id="cb18-4"><a href="#cb18-4" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;<span class="kw">lido:rightsType</span></span>
<span id="cb18-5"><a href="#cb18-5" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">            lido:type=</span><span class="st">&quot;http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00921&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-6"><a href="#cb18-6" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span></span>
<span id="cb18-7"><a href="#cb18-7" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">                rdf:about=</span><span class="st">&quot;https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-8"><a href="#cb18-8" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span><span class="ot"> xml:lang=</span><span class="st">&quot;en&quot;</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-9"><a href="#cb18-9" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                    Public Domain Mark 1.0</span>
<span id="cb18-10"><a href="#cb18-10" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>                &lt;/<span class="kw">skos:prefLabel</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-11"><a href="#cb18-11" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>            &lt;/<span class="kw">skos:Concept</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-12"><a href="#cb18-12" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>        &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsType</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-13"><a href="#cb18-13" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb18-14"><a href="#cb18-14" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;/<span class="kw">lido:rightsWorkWrap</span>&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
            <h4 data-number="4.4.2.2" id="record"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.4.2.2</span> Record</h4>
            <p>The <a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordWrap"><strong>Record
            Wrapper</strong></a> contains information about this very
            LIDO record. It encloses three mandatory elements: &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordID">lido:recordID</a>&gt;
            relates to identifiers from systems where the description
            was produced, &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordType">lido:recordType</a>&gt;
            indicates the description level chosen for the object, and
            &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordSource">lido:recordSource</a>&gt;
            holds data about the producer of this record. Further
            elements relate the identity of the originator, how the LIDO
            record can be referenced in databases or metadata
            repositories, and what rights are claimed by the originator
            for using this record. The rights associated with the record
            are documented in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordRights">lido:recordRights</a>&gt;.</p>
            <p>Please note: Rights specifications in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#recordRights">lido:recordRights</a>&gt;
            refer to all elements of the current LIDO record. It is
            possible to specify different rights for individual object
            description texts in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#descriptiveNoteValue">lido:descriptiveNoteValue</a>&gt;
            using the element &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectDescriptionRights">lido:objectDescriptionRights</a>&gt;
            in the corresponding &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectDescriptionSet">lido:objectDescriptionSet</a>&gt;.
            Rights specifications in &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectDescriptionRights">lido:objectDescriptionRights</a>&gt;
        